# Changelog

If this change is user-facing, add a bullet under `## [Unreleased]` in
`CHANGELOG.md` in the same change. Do not invent a version heading — those
are created only when tagging a release.

User-facing includes: public API, runtime behavior, package identity or
dependencies, consumer docs, and CI/release mechanics a downstream user
would notice.

Skip: internal refactors with no behavior change, test-only work,
comment or formatting-only edits, and private planning files.

Use Keep a Changelog categories (`Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Removed`,
`Deprecated`, `Security`). Write the bullet in user voice, not commit voice.

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
- Updated Directory.Build.props and added MinVer.

<!-- GOOD -->
- Package versions are derived from git tags via MinVer.
```
